                        Win(d)Bag Version 0.2
                        _____________________

    This program plays bagpipe tunes that have been written in the wbg
format.  
    
    This program allows the user to adjust the speed of the melody and  
gracenotes.  Extremely slow gracenote speeds will distort the melody.  
This is because the time it takes to play the gracenote(s) is taken from 
the melody notes they immediately precede.

    A larger number will give a slower pace. Mixed speeds can be 
inputted, e.g. slow melodies with fast gracings or fast melodies with slow 
gracings.  The results are clear.

    After selecting the "Play" radio button there will be four staccato 
quarternotes at the tempo selected.  Once that is done then the bagpipe 
tune starts.  During the playing of the tune the melody and gracenote speed
can be altered by scrolling their respective scroll bars.  The tune may also
be stopped in mid-play by pressing the "pause" radio button.  By pressing 
the "Resume" radio button, the pipe tune resumes.  Selecting the "Stop" 
radio button the tune is reset to the beginning.

    Any comments or suggestions can be e-mailed to (address removed)
Any suggestions for improvement are welcome.


                             Version changes
                             _______________  

                                Win(d)Bag 
                                _________

0.2
                The merging of the the pchanter program and the windbag
        program to make useage easier.
                The changing of buttons from words to images to make usage
        more self-explanatory.
                The changing of the method of looking at the list of the
        pipe tune files.  The index of the files was split according to the
        books that they were translated from.  This was done to make 
        inclusion of new books easier.



